+	// Indexed blend enables (glEnablei/glDisablei) are core only in GLES 3.2 and
+	// otherwise need GL_EXT_draw_buffers_indexed. The guard above lives inside
+	// #ifdef EGL, which the libretro build does not define, so under libretro the
+	// pointers keep whatever the frontend's get_proc_address returned. Apple's
+	// native GLES3 has no glEnablei to hand out (NULL -> the glEnable fallback is
+	// taken), but ANGLE hands back a valid entry point for an ES 3.0 context, where
+	// the call does nothing: GL_BLEND is then NEVER enabled and every alpha-blended
+	// draw becomes an opaque box. Re-apply the guard unconditionally.
+	if (isGLESX && numericVersion < 32 && !ext_draw_buffers_indexed) {
+		ptrEnablei = nullptr;
+		ptrDisablei = nullptr;
+	}
